    "stale_reason": null,
    "text": "I think the club is trying to lower its variance and become harder to beat: a high press, a direct and counter-attacking game, balls over the top for Olusanya, and three physical centre-backs at set plays. The cost has been unforced errors, cheap penalties and getting the players to gel. Thelin's side had a fast start, a long winless run, the Scottish Cup and then a recycled squad; Morris was sold and we lost a main goal threat; injuries and opponents adapting followed. Robinson steadied it. The question is whether the model is now producing a more resilient team, or just a different set of trade-offs.",
